<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39500" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullātus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		3. pullus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>clothed in soiled</i> or <i>black
				garments.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of mourners: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proceres (opp. albatus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 212</span></i>
			.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Prov.: albati ad exsequias, pullati ad nuptias,</span>”
				i. e. <i>who do every thing wrongly</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 5, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Of
			the common people, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 7, 17, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					6, 4, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circulus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 12, 10</span></i>
			; so <i>subst.</i>: ne quis pullatorum, 
			<i>of the common people</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 44</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pullatorum turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 40</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
